==Russian==
{{wp|lang=ru}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|а́ккула|о́кула||dialectal (Northern)}}
* {{alter|ru|а́кула||dialectal (Arkhangelsk)}}

===Etymology===
First attested as {{m|ru|а́ккула|g=f}} in 1747<ref>{{R:ru:SRJa18|а́ккула <small>и</small> акул|38|1|url=01/sl103806}}</ref> and 1789,<ref>{{R:ru:Vasmer|аку́ла}}</ref> {{m|ru|а́ккулъ|g=m}} in 1788,<ref>{{R:ru:Shaposhnikov|акула|22|1}}</ref> {{m|ru|акулъ|g=m}} in 1755.<ref>{{R:ru:Anikin|аку́ла|135|1}}</ref><ref>{{R:uk:ESUM|аку́ла|58|1}}</ref><ref>{{R:ru:Chernykh|аку́ла|35|1}}</ref> Likely {{inh+|ru|zle-mru|-|nocap=1}} (or possibly a [[back-formation]]), attested only as a derivative {{m|zle-mru|акулий|sc=Cyrs}} used to describe liver oil of a [[Greenland shark]] in a source going back to late 16th or early 17th century.<ref>{{R:ru:SRJa1117|акулий|27|1}}</ref>

{{bor+|ru|smi|-}} language (compare {{cog|sms|akkli}}, {{cog|sjd|а̄һклэӈӈк}}, {{cog|se|áhkạlakkis|t=Greenland shark}}), further borrowed {{der|ru|non|hákarl}} (compare {{cog|is|hákarl}} or dialectal {{cog|no|håkall}}).

